📘 eMatch Jira Integration and Custom HTML Report

Created by CAVALHER Erica (EXT)

This documentation explains how the eMatch Katalon project integrates with Jira to publish automated execution results, create or reuse Test Plans, update Test Executions, generate the custom eMatch HTML report, and upload execution attachments.

This version is designed for step by step test cases, not Gherkin.

To make the report visually useful, the test cases must explicitly write the business steps that should appear in the report.
For that reason, the project uses the custom step command:

CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Opened login screen')

When needed, the project can also save controlled evidence images through the custom evidence keyword.

Also important:
the project should use only the ematchReport listener for the custom report flow.
The old failure listener should not be used in this setup.

🎯 What this documentation covers

With this documentation, any maintainer should be able to:

Understand the end to end integration flow
Know how to execute the suites correctly so Jira publication works
Understand how to write visible steps in step by step tests
Know how to generate controlled evidence images
Identify which file is responsible for each part of the process
Know where to change a specific rule
Understand which Jira endpoints are currently active
1. 🚀 How to use the integration

This is the first section because it is the most important one for making the report work correctly.

1.1 Execution model required

To make the custom eMatch report and Jira publication work correctly, you must run:

one main functional test suite
one Jira import test suite
both inside the same Test Suite Collection
in Sequential mode
✅ Required order
Run the real functional suite
Run the Jira import suite after it

The Jira import suite must run second because it reads:

the generated report folder
the execution XML
the custom steps
the start and end times
the evidence images
1.2 Example structure
Main suite
Test Suites/PasserelleBilan/Passerelle Bilan H Bilan French IFRS
Jira import suite
Test Suites/PasserelleBilan/Passerelle Bilan Jira Import
Collection
Passerelle Bilan H Bilan French IFRS Collection
Collection order
Test Suites/PasserelleBilan/Passerelle Bilan H Bilan French IFRS
Test Suites/PasserelleBilan/Passerelle Bilan Jira Import
1.3 What the Jira import suite should contain

The Jira import suite should contain only the test case responsible for publishing the execution to Jira.

Example:

CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraIntegration.jiraImport'('GI5PRD-9877')

This test case is responsible for:

locating the correct report folder
finding the XML result
generating the custom eMatch HTML report
resolving or creating the Jira Test Plan
importing results into Jira
uploading the report and evidences
1.4 Why the collection is necessary

The integration does not work correctly if the Jira import test case is executed alone.

The collection is necessary because:

the functional suite generates the real execution output
the listener captures report metadata during the functional run
the Jira import suite publishes everything after the run finishes

Without the collection, the import may fail to find:

the correct XML
the correct evidence
the correct suite output
the correct report content
2. 🧩 How to make steps appear in the report

This project is built for step by step tests, so the report does not try to guess business steps from technical execution noise.

To make the report readable, the test case must explicitly register the visible steps.

2.1 Step command to use in the test

Use this command whenever you want a step to appear in the report:

CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Opened login screen')
Example
CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Verify set Username and version')
CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Select credentials modal')
CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Select the environment')
CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Opened login screen')
CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraReportSteps.note'('Open login page')
2.2 Rule for writing steps

Good step messages should be:

short
business readable
action oriented
stable over time
Good examples
Opened login screen
Selected environment REC
Confirmed popup
Validated current date
Saved booking changes
Bad examples
click button
line 183 executed
set locator value
call method x



2. Integration Architecture and File Responsibilities

This section explains the actual project structure behind the Jira integration.

JiraFlowCoordinator → Orchestrates the workflow.
JiraTestPlanManager → Resolves or creates Test Plans.
JiraExecutionPublisher → Publishes executions and attachments.
JiraGateway → Calls the endpoints.
JiraReportBuilder → Prepares report data.
JiraHtmlTemplateBuilder → Renders the final HTML.
JiraImagesEvidence → Controls evidence screenshots and evidence folders.
JiraReportSteps → Creates the visible report steps from step by step test cases.
JiraIntegration → Exposes the Jira import keyword used by the test case.
ematchReport → Listener that supports timings, step markers, and report metadata during execution.



3. 🖼️ How to create evidence images

The project can automatically save failure screenshots, and it can also save controlled evidence images when needed.

3.1 Automatic failure evidence

On failed scenarios, the report flow can automatically capture evidence through the integration support classes.

This is used for failed executions and is later attached to:

the HTML report
the Evidence section
the Evidences.zip attachment sent to Jira
3.2 Manual evidence when needed

When you need a specific image during the flow, use the evidence keyword.

Example usage:

CustomKeywords.'jiraIntegration.JiraImagesEvidence.captureNow'('before-save')

Use this only when the scenario needs a very specific checkpoint image.

3.3 Practical rule
Use JiraReportSteps.note() to create visible report steps
Use JiraImagesEvidence.captureNow() only when you really need a manual image
Let the automatic failure capture handle the normal failed evidence flow
4. 🎧 Listener used by the project

This setup should use only one listener for the report orchestration:

✅ Active listener
ematchReport
❌ Do not use in this flow
WindowsFailureScreenshotListener

The custom eMatch reporting flow is already handled by:

ematchReport
JiraReportSteps
JiraImagesEvidence
JiraReportBuilder
JiraHtmlTemplateBuilder

Using another failure listener in parallel can create conflicts or duplicated behavior.

