6. 🔌 Jira endpoints and request objects

This section lists the Jira endpoints and Katalon request objects related to the integration.

1. Import Results

Used to import XML execution results into Jira and create the Test Execution.

Called by:

JiraGateway.importExecutionResults()

Request object:

Jira Integration/Import Results

Review this when:

execution import fails
XML format changes
execution key is not returned
2. Create Test Plan

Used to create a new Jira Test Plan when no valid one exists.

Called by:

JiraGateway.createTestPlan()

Request object:

Jira Integration/Create Test Plan

Review this when:

Jira field mapping changes
Epic field changes
payload needs more fields
3. Search Test Plans

Used to search for existing Test Plans to avoid duplicates.

Called by:

JiraGateway.searchTestPlans()

Review this when:

search returns too many results
expected Test Plan is not found
JQL needs to be refined
4. Get Issue By Key

Used to validate whether a saved Test Plan key still points to the correct Jira issue.

Called by:

JiraGateway.getIssueByKey()

Review this when:

saved key reuse becomes unreliable
validation needs more fields
5. Update Test Plan

Used to link a Test Execution to the resolved Test Plan.

Called by:

JiraGateway.addExecutionToTestPlan()

Request object:

Jira Integration/Update Test Plan

Review this when:

Xray linking rules change
execution association changes
6. Update Test Execution Name

Used to update execution metadata such as summary, labels, and environment.

Called by:

JiraGateway.updateTestExecution()

Request object:

Jira Integration/Update Test Execution Name

Review this when:

execution metadata changes
labels or environment logic changes
7. Evidence attachment

Used to upload files to the Jira Test Execution.

Typical attachments:

custom eMatch HTML report
Results.zip
Evidences.zip

Called by:

JiraGateway.uploadAttachment()

Request object:

Jira Integration/Evidence attachment

Review this when:

